<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warrior of Capestrano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Warrior of Capestrano is a limestone statue of a warrior, more than two metres tall, found in 1934 in a cemetery at Capestrano in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Made in the 6th century BCE, it shows a man in a broad-brimmed hat with breastplate, sword and axe. An inscription in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-picene-language">South Picene language</a> names its maker. It is kept in the National Archaeological Museum of Abruzzo at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chieti">Chieti</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warrior-of-capestrano.jpg" alt="Warrior of Capestrano" width="320" height="732" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerriero_di_capestrano,_da_capestrano,_600-550_ac_ca._02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
